* led12: the 3.3 V rail across the input range.
*
* This deck exists because `rail.power_out.voltage` - what the board promises
* at its 3.3 V rail - was declared in the design and read by nothing. A number
* that looks like a gate and is not one is worse than no number.
*
* It is not a tautology only because the model carries the regulator's dropout
* and its current limit as well as its setpoint: raise the load, or lower the
* input towards 3.3 V, and the rail leaves the band. See models/SOURCE.md.
*
* Every value below comes from the build. @path:end@ is an instance path and
* which end of its resolved range to take.

.include ../models/ldo_3v3.lib

* The regulator, set to the bottom of its own accuracy band - the pessimistic
* end for a rail that has to stay above 3.234 V.
Xldo in out ldo_3v3 vreg=@rail.ldo.v_out:min@

* Input and output capacitors are present for completeness; a DC sweep does
* not exercise them. Startup and stability are not simulated - SOURCE.md says
* why, and they stay on the bring-up list.
Cin in 0 @rail.c_in.capacitance:nom@
Cout out 0 @rail.c_out.capacitance:nom@

* The fixed load that exists so the rail is measurable at all. Through a
* zero-volt source, which is how ngspice reads a current.
Vsense out load 0
Rload load 0 @rail.r_load.resistance:nom@

Vin in 0 12

* Swept a little past both ends, because a measurement taken exactly at the
* edge of the sweep has nothing to interpolate against.
.dc Vin @power.out.voltage:min-0.2@ @power.out.voltage:max+0.2@ 0.05

* The rail itself, at both ends of the input range. Both must sit inside
* `rail.power_out.voltage`.
.meas dc v_rail_at_min_supply FIND v(out) WHEN v(in)=@power.out.voltage:min@
.meas dc v_rail_at_max_supply FIND v(out) WHEN v(in)=@power.out.voltage:max@

* Headroom over the regulator's dropout at the worst input. The part needs
* 260 mV at 40 mA; this board has volts to spare, and the measurement is here
* so that a future input range which does not is caught rather than assumed.
.meas dc tmp_out_min FIND v(out) WHEN v(in)=@power.out.voltage:min@
.meas dc v_dropout_headroom_at_min PARAM='@power.out.voltage:min@-tmp_out_min'

* What the rail actually draws, against the regulator's 150 mA rating.
.meas dc i_load_at_max_supply FIND i(Vsense) WHEN v(in)=@power.out.voltage:max@

.end
